[{"speciesId":"marowak_shadow","fastMove":"MUD_SLAP","chargedMoves":["BONE_CLUB","ROCK_SLIDE"],"weight":10,"editorScore":90,"editorNotes":"Shadow Marowak faces a Mud Slap nerf and more Flying types this season, putting it on the backfoot. It has weathered multiple meta updates in the past, so time will tell if it hangs on. The Shadow version is almost always preferred."},{"speciesId":"moltres_galarian","fastMove":"SUCKER_PUNCH","chargedMoves":["FLY","BRAVE_BIRD"],"weight":12,"editorScore":90,"editorNotes":"Galarian Moltres is a top Flying type in competitive play thanks to its strong matchups against meta defining Ground and Ghost types. It often finds significant neutral play. Its stats are more tempered than its predecessor, Mandibuzz, so it does have to watch for Ice or Rock coverage."},{"speciesId":"clefable","fastMove":"FAIRY_WIND","chargedMoves":["MOONBLAST","METEOR_MASH"],"weight":10,"editorScore":90,"editorNotes":"Clefable is finally finding a place in the metagame with its powerful Charged Attack options. Meteor Mash in particular gives it play into other Fairies and an out against Cradily."},{"speciesId":"blastoise","fastMove":"ROLLOUT","chargedMoves":["HYDRO_CANNON","SKULL_BASH"],"weight":9,"editorScore":90,"editorNotes":"Blastoise is the bulkiest Hydro Cannon user and can augment this even further with Skull Bash. With an excellent balance of stats, power, and speed, it occupies a small but strong spot in the metagame."},{"speciesId":"ninetales_alolan","fastMove":"POWDER_SNOW","chargedMoves":["WEATHER_BALL_ICE","CHILLING_WATER"],"weight":8,"editorScore":90,"editorNotes":"The sims don't always use Chilling Water optimally, so Alolan Ninetales should perform better in some head to head matchups than indicated. Chilling Water is a sidegrade, if not a slight improvement which gives Alolan Ninetales coverage against Fire and broader technical play."},{"speciesId":"lapras","fastMove":"PSYWAVE","chargedMoves":["SPARKLING_ARIA","ICE_BEAM"],"weight":5,"editorScore":90,"editorNotes":"Lapras has a long competitive history, but is currently on its way out of the metagame. It's a poster child for bulky Water types and neutral play. Recent shifts have left it without a clear role, and it now faces stiff competition among Water/Ice types."},{"speciesId":"lapras_shadow","fastMove":"PSYWAVE","chargedMoves":["SPARKLING_ARIA","ICE_BEAM"],"weight":1,"editorScore":90,"editorNotes":"Lapras has a long competitive history, but is currently on its way out of the metagame. It's a poster child for bulky Water types and neutral play. Recent shifts have left it without a clear role as it lacks decisive matchups in the meta."},{"speciesId":"ninetales_alolan_shadow","fastMove":"POWDER_SNOW","chargedMoves":["WEATHER_BALL_ICE","CHILLING_WATER"],"weight":1,"editorScore":90,"editorNotes":"The sims don't always use Chilling Water optimally, so Alolan Ninetales should perform better in some head to head matchups than indicated. Chilling Water is a sidegrade, if not a slight improvement which gives Alolan Ninetales coverage against Fire and broader technical play."},{"speciesId":"lickitung","fastMove":"LICK","chargedMoves":["BODY_SLAM","POWER_WHIP"],"weight":1,"editorScore":85,"editorNotes":"Once a dreaded Great League staple, Lickitung is viable but outclassed by other Normal types, including its evolution, Lickilicky. Lickitung has high bulk but lacks the speed and power to compete in a meta that is becoming increasingly faster."},{"speciesId":"marowak","fastMove":"MUD_SLAP","chargedMoves":["BONE_CLUB","ROCK_SLIDE"],"weight":1,"editorScore":85,"editorNotes":"Marowak is losing ground in the meta, with Gastrodon being preferred for its more neutral typing profile. The Shadow variant is strongly preferred, as its Fast Attack pressure can bulldoze through even negative matchups."},{"speciesId":"wigglytuff","fastMove":"CHARM","chargedMoves":["ICY_WIND","SWIFT"],"weight":20},{"speciesId":"dewgong","fastMove":"ICE_SHARD","chargedMoves":["ICY_WIND","DRILL_RU